{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway","id":1550917,"title":"Why is the Camarilla so crushingly popular on Roll20, anyway?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-10T15:10:46-07:00","id":1550917,"title":"Why is the Camarilla so crushingly popular on Roll20, anyway?","content":"I go on Roll20 and literally every modern day setting vampire game is Camarilla. The only vampire games that aren't Camarilla are set before the Camarilla even existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T16:19:15-07:00","id":1550919,"title":"","content":"If they're open to the public? Because it's the safe option. The Sabbat and Anarchs are more open to concepts that are much harder to mesh into a cohesive player group even when everyone is acting in good faith, and if someone's trying to make a character with intentions that they know are going to be unfun for certain people (either specific people or groups of people) it's much easier to &quot;sneak&quot; them in as justifiable concepts that would be draw into the other main factions.<br /> <br /> It's also a lot easier for sandbox style STs because it's the most &quot;defined&quot; faction in how day-to-day (un)life is supposed to function within a Cam domain. A lot of set-in-the-past settings are still pretty Cam-like in their set up which helps players skip doing a few days of homework looking up specifics about a given time and area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T16:43:09-07:00","id":1550922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway#post1550917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go on Roll20 and literally every modern day setting vampire game is Camarilla. The only vampire games that aren't Camarilla are set before the Camarilla even existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to who?<br /> <br /> I mean the Anarchs are part of the Camarilla prior to 5th Edition.<br /> <br /> There's no other group.<br /> <br /> *Sabbat growls behind locked door*<br /> <br /> No other group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T20:07:03-07:00","id":1550928,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla has always been the most popular setting for Vampire whether on tabletop, LARP, and online. Sabbat players tend to be a passionate, but distinct minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T20:24:58-07:00","id":1550930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway?p=1550928#post1550928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla has always been the most popular setting for Vampire whether on tabletop, LARP, and online. Sabbat players tend to be a passionate, but distinct minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, but even with the hard push to Anarchs, there are zero Anarch games on roll20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T03:20:27-07:00","id":1550935,"title":"","content":"A push with no weight behind it (I'm assuming you mean V5's attempt to refocus the Anarchs as the default PC faction) doesn't accomplish much. All of the reasons why VtM drifted from Anarchs being the default for PCs to the Cam being the default for PCs are present in every edition, including V5. Most Anarch games feel like Cam-lite or Sabbat-lite, and most players would rather just play the non-lite options instead.<br /> <br /> IME the kind of people that should be the main audience for the Anarchs as PCs have grown a strong tendency to just run independent Domains instead... but they're also not people that are likely to put their games up in easily searched places like roll20 either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T08:17:42-07:00","id":1550940,"title":"","content":"As previous mentioned it probably comes down the lack of cohesive distinct identity of the anarchs, they have the aesthetics of dissidence but can't really back it up. On the table this means it makes more sense to gravitate to Camarilla or to a lesser degree, the Sabbat since even if you homebrew your own write it of an actual sect, it only goes as far as your game.<br /> <br /> V5 tried to address but fails because it angle was to try and makes the sword and the tower less appealing, but to quote a friend about marketing &quot;making me think what I like is bad won't make me want what you want.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-11-2025, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T09:34:37-07:00","id":1550941,"title":"","content":"Also, it's not so much that anarchs are part of the Camarilla, it is they are part of the Camarilla's milieu. If you play an anarch, you want to fight against the establishment. The establishment is the Camarilla. An anarch is someone in a domain ruled by a prince defying the elders. I say &quot;defying&quot; because it's not true it's always about &quot;fighting&quot; them. It's not 100% violence and combat. Almost by definition, if you play an anarch you'll be playing in a city ruled by the Camarilla. So the Camarilla's structure still applies. <br /> <br /> Sure, you can run an anarch game set in an anarch domain, but that eliminates something like 90% of why players who want to play anarchs play anarchs. The one published setting of an anarch free state (LABN) does not do a good job making that city interesting to play in. Instead of princes, you have barons. It's Camarilla lite but without the more interesting things about it. And the writers seem to assume that every anarch domain must be exactly like that (even though the whole baron thing was supposed to have grown out of local conditions). No difference in governing philosophies. No variety. There's just an appalling lack of creativity there. If you ever wondering, &quot;Well, what happens after the anarchs win?&quot; That sourcebook seem to say, &quot;The same thing as what happened before.&quot;<br /> <br /> I saw the same thing in LARPs based in anarch domains. Players got bored quickly because the only &quot;plot&quot; that seemed to exist was fighting the Camarilla and the prince. Once that was accomplished, what should they do? Nobody seemed to have any idea. So the STs just went back to creating a &quot;new&quot; plot when every so often some new Camarilla plot/agent would appear so all the players could go against that. Repetitive and boring.<br /> <br /> It's why I've been creating lots of threads recently on running a chronicle set in the Free States. I'm trying to brainstorm things out so I can have a compelling, interesting chronicle dealing with issues that should be addressed in an anarch domain. Have real distinctions between the types of domain governance each group wants. I have a player who loves playing anarchs, but has almost always played in Camarilla games (because that is what the other players wanted even if his character was an anarch type) and been disappointed in the few anarch games he's been in. So I finally want to give him the experience I think he's been waiting for. Hopefully I will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T13:15:51-07:00","id":1550945,"title":"","content":"A somewhat more cynical take is that if you want to play a vampire, you want to play either undead mobsters or sexy people in ball gowns not Lost Boys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T09:53:30-07:00","id":1550961,"title":"","content":"Also, never doubt the power of Lesbian Vampires - \u2018Camarilla\u2019 looks a LOT like \u2018Carmilla\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T11:15:15-07:00","id":1550965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway?p=1550945#post1550945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A somewhat more cynical take is that if you want to play a vampire, you want to play either undead mobsters or sexy people in ball gowns not Lost Boys.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Lost Boys story where the Lost Boys are protagonists could work. It's just that such a movie would need to center some kind of antagonist (if it's not just a Personal Horror story about a gang that spirals into madness and internal conflict due to their individual foibles and vampiric natures). And if there's an antagonist in such a movie, they would need to be either 1) human authorities/hunters, 2) older vampires, 3) a rival gang of Lost Boys, or 4) Something Else.<br /> <br /> And that Something Else is generally the place where Anarch games fumble. The first three at least create plots organically. When Anarchs are left to their own devices, figuring out stuff for them to do requires...significantly more creativity and effort. Creativity and effort neither White Wolf nor Paradox seemed able or willing to muster.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's also the case that when the Anarchs are left to their own devices, the idiosyncrasies of their locale, and the structure (or lack thereof) they adopt, become much more important as the engine of conflict. And that's a lot harder to <i>standardize</i>, without simply recreating the same dynamics of Haves and Have Nots from the Camarilla, but with Barons instead of Princes.<br /> <br /> If your Anarch domain runs on a pure democratic council, with every Lick having their own co-equal vote, how do you actually run that? There are ways, I'm sure. How do you design that model of governance as a framework groups can drop into their own games? Pretty hard. The power blocs at play are much more fluid and person-specific than Camarilla titles or even just Baronies would be. So it's hard to generalize.<br /> <br /> And if you - the hypothetical designer of a City by Night book where this model is in play - manage to pull off an interesting and playable dynamic, you still run the risk of the particulars of that domain just being copy-pasted to all similar domains. The Chicago By Night problem all over again, where the most popular classic depiction of a Camarilla domain becomes the template everyone replicates.<br /> <br /> (Not that this would necessarily be BAD, since you'd have at least one functional model for an Anarch domain, that isn't just Camarilla-lite. It would get repetitive, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T20:11:23-07:00","id":1550982,"title":"","content":"The best thing that could happen to Anarch domains as a concept would be a book devoted to explore a variety of options. Something similar to a <i>By Night</i>, but with four to six unrelated cities instead of just one. Less word-count on a given city, sure, but a better feel of what an Anarch domain can be like and how they can differ.<br /> <br /> But for Roll 20 I'd say the big problem is really what kinds of games will be public games. Anything Anarch or Sabbath is more likely to be closed, and in fact I don't think an open Sabbath game would attract the best kind of players if done publicly. Without access to the site's internal data, we can't really say what kind of game is more common there, or how much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T04:46:08-07:00","id":1550985,"title":"","content":"Even if we had roll20's data on private games... how much does one site really mean? A lot of WoD fans looking to play online don't really have a particular reason to use roll20 outside of it being a popular site to find games with unfamiliar players/groups. If I'm just running VtM for a few friends online because meeting up in person is difficult or practically impossible, a program like Discord has every tool I need. Maybe in a particularly combat heavy game I might add in some free Google stuff (spreadsheets for tracking initiative, active effects, and spent resources, and a drawing to doodle a basic map for players to orient their characters in the scene) that I can either link to live or put in group VC screen share.<br /> <br /> How many people are playing the game in zero-visibility parts of the Internet because they can get all the tools they want for free and they aren't actively looking for new players? No idea and I don't think there's really a way to find out that would tell use what people are actually playing..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T10:41:55-07:00","id":1551002,"title":"","content":"In this particular case, Roll20's data is relevant just because it was the initial question, but yes. My current Mage chronicle itself is being run on Discord. Roll20 is probably a very small portion of online games going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T07:09:16-07:00","id":1551039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway?p=1550982#post1550982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best thing that could happen to Anarch domains as a concept would be a book devoted to explore a variety of options. Something similar to a <i>By Night</i>, but with four to six unrelated cities instead of just one. Less word-count on a given city, sure, but a better feel of what an Anarch domain can be like and how they can differ.<br /> <br /> But for Roll 20 I'd say the big problem is really what kinds of games will be public games. Anything Anarch or Sabbath is more likely to be closed, and in fact I don't think an open Sabbath game would attract the best kind of players if done publicly. Without access to the site's internal data, we can't really say what kind of game is more common there, or how much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While I agree broadly, does this not lead to self segregation and therefore marginalization? I see it with my own groups, it feels like you are just swimming in your own little pond...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T22:00:03-07:00","id":1551059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway?p=1551039#post1551039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While I agree broadly, does this not lead to self segregation and therefore marginalization? I see it with my own groups, it feels like you are just swimming in your own little pond...</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but is the risk worth taking?<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, it's a game. Having a good time is far more important, specially from a personal standpoint, than advocating for your play style by playing publicly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T00:40:56-07:00","id":1551060,"title":"","content":"Additionally, while it is to our collective benefits as fans for more people to play the game abstractly... it's literally Paradox's job to get people to buy the game. <br /> <br /> Paradox has seemed to go completely silent on any attempt to support fans running games in public venues (either in person at conventions, or online on bigger sites like Roll20)... though I'll admit that last I heard anyone over there say something about it was when Martin was still in charge of the WoD. Word of mouth is extremely strong in TTRPG sales, and investing in getting people to run your game publicly really isn't a big investment (lots of smaller companies than Paradox manage). <br /> <br /> While I've been out of the con circuit for a bit now, it's always obvious which games at cons are being run by passionate fans that pour a lot into a game they love, and which are that but with a product that actually supports their efforts (Paizo's success with Pathfinder included a lot of that). Most people are casual players because there is so much competition for our time and attention, and most people are going to gravitate towards products that feel supported.<br /> <br /> I really do think there is a lack of appreciation by a lot of publishers for what it means for someone putting themselves out there as a fan running their games to have things like branded GM screens, dice, official modules with nice character sheets for all the premades, etc. means for attracting people to play. Potential players react to that kind of perception of company investment.<br /> <br /> The onus on us, as the fans, shouldn't be to carry the brand on our backs. A lot of us will anyway, because we're fans, but fans can't stop a fading brand from fading on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T17:23:33-07:00","id":1551144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway?p=1551059#post1551059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but is the risk worth taking?<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, it's a game. Having a good time is far more important, specially from a personal standpoint, than advocating for your play style by playing publicly.</div> </div> </div> </div>see, this is where i am torn as well. I remember well how my ST played with me in a group in the early days and looking back he did not have to either. From my point of view we all are learning from the ones before us.<br /> <br /> I disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> as little bit as well, as i agree that it is on the company to create a game i want to play (which is not the case with V5). However there was a sense of community, a sense of belonging with V:TM that i am not feeling right now, but that i do miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T18:59:02-07:00","id":1551147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550917-why-is-the-camarilla-so-crushingly-popular-on-roll20-anyway?p=1551144#post1551144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">see, this is where i am torn as well. I remember well how my ST played with me in a group in the early days and looking back he did not have to either. From my point of view we all are learning from the ones before us.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood, I think.<br /> <br /> This is not about newbies, it's about destructive players.<br /> <br /> Simply put, Sabbath games attract destructive players and makes them feel they can be their worse. There's a strong, healthy community of Sabbath players, don't get me wrong.<br /> <br /> But when you receive a new player at your table, there's always the risk of bringing a bad player, and in public spaces this is worsened a lot. Specially on the internet.<br /> <br /> A bad player, not in a &quot;don't know how to play&quot; sense, but in an &quot;actively trolls the other players&quot; sense, can be <u><b>extremely</b></u> disruptive and make for an ugly experience for everyone.<br /> <br /> More so because playing inhuman characters actually takes a lot of vulnerability from some players, and the ST has to be aware of that. Being inhuman to fictional characters is cathartic. Being inhuman to fellow players is just bullying. And bullies gravitate to such opportunities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T05:26:20-07:00","id":1551153,"title":"","content":"You are right, i thought you were talking about both anarch and Sabbat games. After reading your original message i see that while you were talking about both at the start of your post, you specified later.<br /> <br /> I do like Sabbat games, but i do agree that they tend to be handled differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T16:27:45-07:00","id":1551207,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with playing the Sabbat once in awhile and we would probably try to play the pack as intelligent monsters who know what tactics would be smart and not be mindless shovel heads. Maybe maturity is required in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-29T15:28:46-07:00","id":1551337,"title":"","content":"Sabbat fall into the same &quot;problem group&quot; of character options (alongside Malkavians, Rogues, and any Chaotic alignment), wherein they are <i>interpreted</i> by certain immature players as giving them license to be as disruptive as their little hearts desire with no consequences.<br /> <br /> In truth, all of these, along with every other character option in every TTRPG, requires a base level of consideration for one's fellow players and GM.<br /> <br /> It's a lot easier for problem players to get away with disruptive behavior in a pick-up game type setting, versus an established group where your peers at the table (physical or virtual) have to actually LIKE you and want to play with you. Sabbat pick-up games, therefore, are the worst of both worlds. Attracting a greater percentage of the immature playerbase, AND coming with the assumption on their part that it's a game where they're &quot;allowed&quot; to be a dick. (This despite Sabbat packs, in-universe, actually having the greatest justification among Vampire coteries for being close-knit; the Vinculum and all that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}